riscv64 zkVM: emit listed precompile P/Invokes as a single CSR write

On ZisK a precompile runs when a CSR is written with the address of its operand block;
libziskos exposes each as a two-instruction function (csrs; ret) that managed code calls
through a P/Invoke (for a LibraryImport, through the generated "<entrypoint>g____PInvoke"
local function). In the traced Nethermind block keccak-f ran 141k times and sha256-f 27k
times: each paid the auipc+jalr pair and the stub, and, because a call kills every
caller-saved register, the hashing wrappers kept their pointers and counters in sN
registers with the matching prolog/epilog traffic.

JitZkCsrPInvokes (a ','-separated list of "entrypoint:csr", csr in hex; empty by default)
names the P/Invokes to emit as `csrrs x0, csr, aN` in place of the call. The call node
stays a call for everything that matters to correctness - argument setup in a0, ordering
against the stores that fill and the loads that read the operand block - but LSRA gets an
empty kill set for it, codegen emits the CSR write instead of the call sequence, and the
leaf RA-elision scan no longer counts it as a call. bflat passes
"syscall_keccak_f:800,syscall_sha256_f:805" for the zisk libc.

Measured on nine mainnet blocks with ziskemu against the same build without the knob:
-0.43% executed steps (-6.9M), identical outputs; every one of the 25 managed call sites
became a single csrrs and ValueKeccak.Compute lost its four callee-saved registers.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
index 93b9ce074..81c381e1b 100644
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
@@ -6037,6 +6037,18 @@ void CodeGen::genCall(GenTreeCall* call)
 //
 void CodeGen::genCallInstruction(GenTreeCall* call)
 {
+    // zkVM: a listed precompile P/Invoke is the CSR write itself (see JitZkCsrPInvokes). The
+    // single argument, the operand address, is already in its ABI register; no call, no
+    // return value, no registers changed, and nothing for the GC to see.
+    const int zkCsr = m_compiler->zkCsrForPInvoke(call);
+    if (zkCsr >= 0)
+    {
+        const ABIPassingSegment& seg = call->gtArgs.GetArgByIndex(0)->AbiInfo.Segment(0);
+        assert(seg.IsPassedInRegister());
+        GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R_I(INS_csrrs, EA_8BYTE, REG_ZERO, seg.GetRegister(), zkCsr);
+        return;
+    }
+
     // Determine return value size(s).
     const ReturnTypeDesc* pRetTypeDesc = call->GetReturnTypeDesc();
     EmitCallParams        params;
@@ -7160,7 +7172,11 @@ void CodeGen::genComputeLeafRaElision()
     {
         for (GenTree* const node : LIR::AsRange(block))
         {
-            if ((node->OperIs(GT_CALL) && !node->AsCall()->IsFastTailCall()) || node->OperIs(GT_JMP, GT_INTRINSIC))
+            // zkVM: a precompile P/Invoke emitted as a CSR write (JitZkCsrPInvokes) is not a call
+            // and leaves RA alone.
+            if ((node->OperIs(GT_CALL) && !node->AsCall()->IsFastTailCall() &&
+                 (m_compiler->zkCsrForPInvoke(node->AsCall()) < 0)) ||
+                node->OperIs(GT_JMP, GT_INTRINSIC))
             {
                 return;
             }
