+// riscv64 zkVM (ZisK): a precompile runs when a CSR is written with the address of its
+// operand block. libziskos wraps each one in a two-instruction function (csrs; ret) that
+// managed code reaches through a P/Invoke, so one keccak-f costs the call pair, the stub,
+// and in the caller every callee-saved register the call forces live values into. Entries
+// "entrypoint:csr" (csr in hex, ','-separated) name the P/Invokes to emit as a single
+// `csrrs x0, csr, aN` instead: no call, no stub, and no register kills, since the CSR write
+// changes no general register. Empty (the default) leaves every P/Invoke a call.
+RELEASE_CONFIG_STRING(JitZkCsrPInvokes, "JitZkCsrPInvokes")
